      "body_recovery_method": "wayback",
      "context_excerpt": "The UK-LLM project, established in 2023 as BritLLM and led by University College London, has previously released two models for U.K. languages. Its new model for Welsh, developed in collaboration with Wales’ Bangor University and NVIDIA, aligns with Welsh government efforts to boost the active use of the language, with the goal of achieving a million speakers by 2050 — an initiative known as Cymraeg 2050 .",
